 "name": "walkway_lab",
 "_comment": "The height-stack lab (walkway-lab round): a pure 22% slope with the stack's record types staged SIDE BY SIDE along Z, one claim per stage, judged with RT_GROUND_PROBES=1 posts (base at the analytic height \u2014 buried/floating posts localize any mesh disagreement instantly). S0 z<-65: bare slope. S1 z~-50: one PAD. S2 z~-15: one RAMP climbing the hill. S3 z~15: the PRIORITY LADDER (pad 2 inside road 1 inside grade -1). S4 z~45: the TERRACE LIP (two adjacent grade planes 5 m apart). S5a z~70: a walkway riding S2-style graded ground (must sit flush). S5b z~95: a walkway CROSSING an S4-style lip (the known-impossible flat band; must stair or reroute when lip-aware routing lands).",
